                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "233153731",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198133215341",
                            "num_reviews": 97,
                            "playtime_forever": 526,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 221,
                            "playtime_at_review": 73,
                            "last_played": 1793792354
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]A glitchy port of a mobile game and nothing more[/h1]\nThe game as a whole is honestly a mess. The UI is terrible, the controls feel poorly adapted for PC, and there's a particularly annoying issue where the game switches to keyboard-only controls as soon as you press a key. After that, the mouse simply stops working, and the only way I've found to get it back is to restart the entire game. It's the kind of basic issue that should have been caught before release.\n\nThe gameplay itself doesn't really offer anything interesting either. It feels like a fairly basic mobile game that was brought to Steam without doing much to make it feel like an actual PC release. Even the UI icons are reused for completely different actions, which comes across as incredibly lazy and makes things more confusing than they need to be.\n\nThe achievements also appear to be bugged, which only adds to the feeling that the game wasn't properly tested before being released.\n\nAnd then there's the Steam rating. Looking at the reviews, I genuinely have a hard time believing the current rating is representative of the actual game. It honestly looks like a wave of botted fake reviews to me. There's no way this game deserves the overwhelmingly positive reception it's getting. At best, this should be sitting somewhere around Mixed.\n\nOverall, there's not much here to recommend. A poorly adapted mobile game with buggy controls, a terrible UI, questionable achievements and very little interesting gameplay. It feels more like a quick cash grab than a proper PC release.\n[list]\n[*]♉ For more reviews like this, check out my [b][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/10745643/]curator page[/url][/b].\n[/list]",
